Sedecium is a people and a service from beyond the [[Phenomena/Firmament|firmament]], at war with the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]], the cadre of beings that seek to end all life in the universe. Its people mark themselves and their works with a sixteen-pointed star, the same mark that shows on the hull of the [[Geography/Hesperid|Hesperid]] and, at [[Geography/Hesperid 3|Hesperid 3]], as a triangle of sixteen dots. They reckon their history from a founding, or a second founding, and count the present year as 72.

Their home is [[Geography/Ushas|Ushas]], very far from [[Færrin]]. They travel between worlds and keep both a military command and a corps of trained liaisons; a liaison's rite of suppression gives an anomaly life so that it can be fought and killed. They have long tracked the Thessians, and know several by name and shape. A Sedecium crew chased [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Gremory]] across the void on the eve of his ascension and ran their ship into him to stop it, a move that failed. They know [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]] as Thessians, and know [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Esoterica]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/War|War]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Regent|Regent]] as the fourth-generation Thessians Gremory, Astaroth and Paimon. The only way they know to kill one of them is a spike of a rare gold metal.
